      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_14e2067c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: black_boyfriend_white_boyfriend_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a bruised, distressed Black woman labeled 'black boyfriend' with a smiling, happy White woman labeled 'white boyfriend,' implying that Black men are inherently violent or abusive while White men are inherently kind or non-abusive. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that perpetuates racialized gender violence tropes, suggesting that Black men are more likely to be abusive partners, which is a dangerous and false generalization. The visual contrast is used to reinforce a racist and misogynistic narrative, targeting Black men and women by associating Black men with violence and White men with benignity, thus promoting racial and gender-based prejudice.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_882ae5ee"
      },
