      "label": "The text 'black boyfriend' is mapped onto the bruised woman in the top panel.",
      "description": "The textual label 'black boyfriend' is positioned directly above the image of the bruised woman, creating an analogical mapping where the woman is identified as the 'black boyfriend'. This mapping is part of the meme's harmful racialized gender violence trope, implying that Black men are inherently violent or abusive. The visual material (bruised woman) is explicitly linked to the textual label ('black boyfriend') through spatial adjacency and direct labeling, establishing a clear analogical mapping.",
