      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cdc4d507",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience for this meme is individuals who hold or are exposed to racially and gendered stereotypes, particularly those who may unconsciously or consciously endorse the harmful trope that Black men are inherently more likely to be abusive partners while White men are inherently kind or non-abusive. The meme is designed to appeal to audiences who are familiar with or reinforce racial binaries and misogynistic narratives, often found in online communities that propagate hate speech, racialized gender violence tropes, and white savior complex ideologies. The visual contrast and labeling are intended to resonate with viewers who interpret the image through the lens of these pre-existing prejudices, making it particularly effective in communities that normalize or celebrate such stereotypes.",
